    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L15-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "15.3: Double the Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can find the amplitude and midline of a trigonometric function using the graph or from an equation. For example, let’s look at the function given by the equation \\(y = 3\\cos\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) + 2\\). We can see that the…",
