      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L15-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "15.3: Double the Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Notice that the graph of \\(y=\\cos(2\\theta)\\) has the same general shape as the graph of \\(y =\\cos(\\theta)\\) (same midline and amplitude) but the waves are compressed together. And what if we wanted to give the graph of cosine a stretched…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l15.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L15-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "15.3: Double the Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The maximum distance of the values of a periodic function above or below the midline.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l15.rich-lesson-v2.json",
